// Refused blob attaches, per kind and reason.
// Backs the "saves are refusing files" alert: a save that names a blob it may not attach is refused
// with the reason as the cause. An expired upload or a duplicate in one payload is a user's slip and
// a handful is normal; a burst of one reason on one kind is a client defect (a stale id, the wrong
// kind), a client that attaches another user's uploads, or saves racing for one blob (persist).
// More than 20 of one reason on one kind in the window is a starting point.
customMetrics
| where name == "tellma.blobs.attach.rejected"
| extend kind = tostring(customDimensions["kind"])
| extend reason = tostring(customDimensions["reason"])
| summarize rejected = sum(valueSum) by kind, reason, bin(timestamp, 15m)
| where rejected > 20
